<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Road Conditions: Our access route is a well-maintained, hard-packed dirt road. While 4x4 vehicles are not essential, we advise against bringing sports cars due to their lower clearance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Services En-Route: Be aware that along Tx-118 between Alpine and Study Butte, services are sparse. There aren't any gas stations or stores, and cell service can be patchy. Ensure your vehicle has a full tank and is in tip-top shape before embarking on this stretch.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Hydration is Key: Big Bend region can be dry and hot. Always carry plenty of water with you, especially if you're planning on hiking or other outdoor activities.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
